  "name": "session-end transactions have crash windows that strand orphan active sessions",
  "slug": "session-end-transactions-have-crash",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "session-end transactions have crash windows that strand orphan active sessions",
    "details_md": "start/stop perform 2-4 independent writes under one lock with no journal: crash after createSession but before updateTicket leaves an ended_at:null session no ticket references (renders active forever); takeover ends the previous session LAST, so a crash strands the seized session too. stop's window self-heals; these two do not. Consider write-ordering (ticket last) + a repair path in reindex.",
    "acceptance": [
      "orphaned ended_at:null sessions are detectable/repairable (reindex --heal or similar)",
      "takeover write order closes the old session before the point of no return"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/start.ts:202",
      "src/cli/commands/stop.ts:111"
    ],
